ONE REVIEW. Adversarial. Do not fix anything. Answer in under 400 words.

Review a CLAIM before it drives work, not a diff.

Setting: legoESM OMIP run on the eORCA1 tripole, scored against NEMO 5.0.1
ORCA1 as oracle. Equatorial Pacific box, |lat|<=2, 200-260E, 660 columns.
Our side is an INSTANTANEOUS snapshot; NEMO's is a FIVE-DAY MEAN record.
Measured at two days (25 and 30) against the matched records (4 and 5).
Probe: scripts/validate/ocean_fidelity/equatorial_diffusivity_oracle.py
Card:  scripts/cluster/omip_nemo/_eq_prandtl_oracle.sbatch
Ours from snapshot K_M_diag / K_H_diag; NEMO from grid_W avm / avt.

The numbers (median over the box, m2/s):
  surface 5-65 m      ours avm 0.0019 -> 6.37e-06 between d25 and d30
                      NEMO avm 0.0087 -> 0.00168
  entrainment 65-105m ours avm 3.11e-06 -> 3.04e-06 ; NEMO 2.53e-06 -> 2.45e-06
                      ours avt 5.37e-07 -> 3.44e-07 ; NEMO 1.13e-06 -> 1.12e-06
  deep background     ours avm 3.01e-06 avt 2.13e-07 ; NEMO avm 2.30e-06 avt 9.05e-07
  convective fraction ours 0.000 at every depth ; NEMO up to 0.90 at 1 m,
                      0.058-0.082 at 65-105 m

The claim, in four parts:
1. The surface band is UNUSABLE because our value moves a factor 300 between
   the two days and NEMO's own five-day mean moves a factor 5.2.
2. The 65-105 m band IS usable because both sides move about 3% there.
3. In that band our VISCOSITY matches (1.23x, 1.24x) so vertical viscosity is
   NOT the carrier of a separate finding that our equatorial undercurrent is
   a third to a half of NEMO's; but our HEAT DIFFUSIVITY is 0.31-0.48x, i.e.
   the closure's momentum/heat PARTITION is wrong rather than its magnitude.
4. This explains a separate surface heat budget which found we put ~30 W/m2
   LESS heat into this box than NEMO while running 1.15 C too warm: heat
   leaves a tropical surface layer downward, and our downward heat diffusivity
   is a third of the oracle's.

Attack these specifically:
(a) Is a median over 660 columns of an instantaneous field comparable to a
    median of a five-day mean, given a diffusivity is intermittent and
    lognormal? Does averaging order (mean-of-median vs median-of-mean) break
    part 2 or part 3?
(b) Our convective fraction is 0.000 everywhere while NEMO's is 0.90 at the
    surface. Does that mean our enhanced-vertical-diffusion / convection path
    is not firing at all here, and if so does it contaminate part 3?
(c) Are K_M_diag / K_H_diag sampled at the same point in the timestep as
    NEMO's avm / avt (before or after the implicit solve, before or after
    any convective adjustment)? If not, what does that do to the ratios?
(d) Our deep Prandtl number is 13.9 while NEMO's documented mapping caps it
    at 10. Is that a real inconsistency in our background coefficients, or an
    artifact of comparing a ratio of medians to a median of ratios?
(e) Does part 4 survive? Name any step where the sign or the magnitude does
    not follow.

Say which parts you would REJECT and what single measurement would settle it.
